Hint: Write out the variance as much as you can, then look for quantities with known values. We start from$$
ewcommand{\Var}{	ext{Var}}
ewcommand{\E}{\mathbb{E}}
ewcommand{\Cov}{	ext{Cov}}\Var[X-Y]=\E[(X-Y)^2]-(\E[X-Y])^2.$$Now, we can multiply these out and use linearity of the expectation to get:$$\Var[X-Y]=\E[X^2]-2\E[XY]+\E[Y^2]-(\E[X])^2+2\E[X]\E[Y]-(\E[Y])^2.$$Now, we know the values for $\Var[X]=\E[X^2]-(\E[X])^2$, $\Var[Y]=\E[Y^2]-(\E[Y])^2$, and $\Cov[X,Y]=\E[XY]-\E[X]\E[Y]$. Can you see how to rewrite $\Var[X-Y]$ in terms of those functions?

Ok, one way to intimidate students is to use large numbers like 6000 in questions. A simple tool to beat this strategy of examiner is to replace the big number by a generic symbol say $n$. We thus calculate the limit $$f(n) = \lim_{x 	o 0} rac{x^{n} - \sin^{n}x}{x^{2}\sin^{n}x}$$ where $n$ is a positive integer. The answer for the question is $f(6000)$. We have egin{align}f(n) &= \lim_{x 	o 0} rac{x^{n} - \sin^{n}x}{x^{2}\sin^{n}x}
otag\&= \lim_{x 	o 0}\dfrac{x - \sin x}{x^{3}\cdot\dfrac{\sin x}{x}}\cdot\dfrac{{\displaystyle \sum_{i = 0}^{n - 1}x^{i}\sin^{n - 1 - i}x}}{\sin^{n - 1}x}
otag\&= \lim_{x 	o 0} rac{x - \sin x}{x^{3}}\sum_{i = 0}^{n - 1}\left( rac{x}{\sin x}ight)^{i}
otag\&= \sum_{i = 0}^{n - 1} 1\cdot \lim_{x 	o 0} rac{1 - \cos x}{3x^{2}}	ext{ (via L'Hospital's Rule)}
otag\&=  rac{n}{6}
otag\end{align}and hence the desired answer is $f(6000) = 1000$.

